ived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spiderpoul/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spiderpoul/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spiderpoul/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spiderpoul","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/commits/dfa0f914af9ed45e81553972d9f9f9ec5279addc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:17:13Z","email":"spiderpoul@mail.ru","name":"Pavel Uvarov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:17:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"presentation: harness 10/90, quality gates, Chrome DevTools MCP, CommonJS example (#78)\n\n* presentation: harness 10/90, quality gates, Chrome DevTools MCP and CommonJS example\n\n- New slide \"Agent = Model + Harness\" with harness-anatomy.png from Google''s\n  \"The New SDLC with Vibe Coding\" (10% model, 90% harness), mapped to the blocks.\n- The \"correct example\" trap is now CommonJS instead of useAutoTrimCells:\n  root Babel with modules: ''cjs'' adds 2.5 MB to the users-and-roles entry\n  (8.4 vs 5.9 MB, measured) and turns import() into require().\n- Docs slide: a new outdated-vs-current example (memoize everything vs measure).\n- Block 6 rebuilt as quality gates: four levels, how to build gates the agent\n  cannot bypass, mandatory agent review in CI with profile reviewers for\n  critical paths via CODEOWNERS, and Chrome DevTools MCP / Web Vitals as an\n  extra guardrail with real check and trace output.\n- Removed both quizzes, the check-message slide and the SDD backup slides;\n  \"Ready-made skills\" moved back into the skills block.\n- Markdown files with tables render as previews inside the file frame, so the\n  tables are readable; Run A / Run B columns are colour-coded.\n- Commit links point to the rebuilt demo/agent-ready-v2 (new step 7).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012aDpb8QQeuah31M5196RHG\n\n* presentation: animated HTML/CSS harness diagram instead of the picture\n\nThe Agent = Model + Harness slide draws the layers itself: LLM core,\nthe harness ring with Instructions, Tools & MCP, Orchestration and\nGuardrails, Evals on its edge and the platform ring outside. Each click\nlights one layer and the note on the right explains it and names the\nblock of the talk; the last click fills the 10/90 bar.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012aDpb8QQeuah31M5196RHG\n\n* presentation: both runs get the same good spec\n\nRun A and Run B now receive one prompt and one spec, byte-identical in\nboth demo branches, so the comparison isolates the repository setup and\nnobody can say B just got a better prompt. The start slide shows the\nshared prompt, the good-spec slide says both runs get it, the bad spec\nstays as an anti-example only, and the result tables no longer credit\nthe spec to Run B. Commit links point to the rewritten demo branch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012aDpb8QQeuah31M5196RHG\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2de8396faaf8439ae16c64d679cb0981083c613b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/git/trees/2de8396faaf8439ae16c64d679cb0981083c613b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/git/commits/dfa0f914af9ed45e81553972d9f9f9ec5279addc","verification":{"payload":"tree 2de8396faaf8439ae16c64d679cb0981083c613b\nparent 151e3abe4292fe1a8fe5a43bc741b712d340cdea\nauthor Pavel Uvarov <spiderpoul@mail.ru> 1790792233 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790792233 +0300\n\npresentation: harness 10/90, quality gates, Chrome DevTools MCP, CommonJS example (#78)\n\n* presentation: harness 10/90, quality gates, Chrome DevTools MCP and CommonJS example\n\n- New slide \"Agent = Model + Harness\" with harness-anatomy.png from Google''s\n  \"The New SDLC with Vibe Coding\" (10% model, 90% harness), mapped to the blocks.\n- The \"correct example\" trap is now CommonJS instead of useAutoTrimCells:\n  root Babel with modules: ''cjs'' adds 2.5 MB to the users-and-roles entry\n  (8.4 vs 5.9 MB, measured) and turns import() into require().\n- Docs slide: a new outdated-vs-current example (memoize everything vs measure).\n- Block 6 rebuilt as quality gates: four levels, how to build gates the agent\n  cannot bypass, mandatory agent review in CI with profile reviewers for\n  critical paths via CODEOWNERS, and Chrome DevTools MCP / Web Vitals as an\n  extra guardrail with real check and trace output.\n- Removed both quizzes, the check-message slide and the SDD backup slides;\n  \"Ready-made skills\" moved back into the skills block.\n- Markdown files with tables render as previews inside the file frame, so the\n  tables are readable; Run A / Run B columns are colour-coded.\n- Commit links point to the rebuilt demo/agent-ready-v2 (new step 7).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012aDpb8QQeuah31M5196RHG\n\n* presentation: animated HTML/CSS harness diagram instead of the picture\n\nThe Agent = Model + Harness slide draws the layers itself: LLM core,\nthe harness ring with Instructions, Tools & MCP, Orchestration and\nGuardrails, Evals on its edge and the platform ring outside. Each click\nlights one layer and the note on the right explains it and names the\nblock of the talk; the last click fills the 10/90 bar.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012aDpb8QQeuah31M5196RHG\n\n* presentation: both runs get the same good spec\n\nRun A and Run B now receive one prompt and one spec, byte-identical in\nboth demo branches, so the comparison isolates the repository setup and\nnobody can say B just got a better prompt. The start slide shows the\nshared prompt, the good-spec slide says both runs get it, the bad spec\nstays as an anti-example only, and the result tables no longer credit\nthe spec to Run B. Commit links point to the rewritten demo branch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012aDpb8QQeuah31M5196RHG\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvVIqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASaIQACXajmGhh6hx2bJlPKQFindO\nMM53c6r/4HuKSfEOjjzM9hwDEg3PLIaQfdwKunjxVcu7jGsB0gA9ce6HhIsKZwLA\nShG8TSLxe1tXVQDGKrBj8xT6iq/LLUqRPjidpWfyy948Jd1VnXSM2FBQpsKEGZnV\nXO0ngrWca9OklHDJsesVDVHblPc1NKXzXJNc49gGuBKGMWkaVu1KFX6BdUgxV4nX\n5YH0Y9XxbHqCws7pjhXmmXWygDNey9KOypN7u8WYEgUZx7rmToxYBthi2jRo67iV\nHn1JH6+2EjNYqDm+MM6zlvcTGkHmESJJ4Q7BPvzJ1B6To8373RVTs1hdjiTm+8rX\ndUA8Z7XBOAZM56MVgAzhx80ph1nnpVhsYT5Xd9TArX7PiB8cDxKFJjRuc5LgqK9Q\ndCOFzXO9y1LlBsWBNnNi2kjTyU5nPRzEq0L0INauBYI7IyFcFh48umoaTyDroy4Z\nEhRaOoTOiBAFMlWgp/j8LpzDGwJQqF1NA8O/LTgEfVoHW3IKjRo8Ne+qCLSiGQh9\nymq+ogVhbbcUUznVc0jJchor+sS2kqJA2J1Ig4pCuNkddcDnz1rC/tAKEKvJmt2O\noMljl2wxe6BCNIvRbLMUGF24qj1oqJuUn/+QFg99lPinX4p5/vwmQnX3hDGbb1a1\nxlKItm8jtPhp8NK/605S\n=8jk+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T18:17:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":