presentation: rebuild the talk around predictability for internal models\n\nThe talk now argues that weak internal models fail because the project\nis not set up, and shows every harness block as annotated files from the\nRussian demo branch, followed by a switch to the commit that added them:\n\n- opening poll about internal models and why teams don''t use them;\n- annotated AGENTS.md, a nested AGENTS.md for the shell registry and\n  proxy, and a counter-example;\n- documentation walkthrough, SDD in legacy with CodeSpeak and levels of\n  SDD, a good and a bad spec;\n- \"where does this belong\" quiz, useful and ready-made skills with\n  links, performance-check walkthrough and a bad skill;\n- subagent quiz and how explorer gets invoked;\n- check messages as prompts and path-based reviewers for critical code;\n- a new evals block: why, anatomy, bad and good case, adoption steps;\n- results, a checklist for your own project and the closing message.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B4EJbsQcayZ3jP7YvPBS6Q","tree":{"sha":"1a5a7485c786a5ecb09c53c4bbac56748e41d4e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/git/trees/1a5a7485c786a5ecb09c53c4bbac56748e41d4e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/git/commits/ee4afe324ade016789fc591969b12f1e419ba11c","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a5a7485c786a5ecb09c53c4bbac56748e41d4e1\nparent 186f075e5a1b14592562c07c5501093fd4b4c32e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790248397 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790249240 +0000\n\npresentation: rebuild the talk around predictability for internal models\n\nThe talk now argues that weak internal models fail because the project\nis not set up, and shows every harness block as annotated files from the\nRussian demo branch, followed by a switch to the commit that added them:\n\n- opening poll about internal models and why teams don''t use them;\n- annotated AGENTS.md, a nested AGENTS.md for the shell registry and\n  proxy, and a counter-example;\n- documentation walkthrough, SDD in legacy with CodeSpeak and levels of\n  SDD, a good and a bad spec;\n- \"where does this belong\" quiz, useful and ready-made skills with\n  links, performance-check walkthrough and a bad skill;\n- subagent quiz and how explorer gets invoked;\n- check messages as prompts and path-based reviewers for critical code;\n- a new evals block: why, anatomy, bad and good case, adoption steps;\n- results, a checklist for your own project and the closing message.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B4EJbsQcayZ3jP7YvPBS6Q\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEK3QgK+\nqdta2x+QrBeNyZPypnLP6eeLfphjJUWHMQvCfKyLJHpnDbJl5B20wMipdND0H7pihK4W+KQqv2L1\n6AE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T11:27:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/commit/ee4afe324ade016789fc591969b12f1e419ba11c","node_id":"C_kwDOP1Nl89oAKGVlNGFmZTMyNGFkZTAxNjc4OWZjNTkxOTY5YjEyZjFlNDE5YmExMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/commit/186f075e5a1b14592562c07c5501093fd4b4c32e","sha":"186f075e5a1b14592562c07c5501093fd4b4c32e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/commits/186f075e5a1b14592562c07c5501093fd4b4c32e"}],"sha":"ee4afe324ade016789fc591969b12f1e419ba11c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/commits/ee4afe324ade016789fc591969b12f1e419ba11c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23116531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spiderpoul/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spiderpoul/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spiderpoul/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spiderpoul/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/spiderpoul","id":23116531,"login":"spiderpoul","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMTE2NTMx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spiderpoul/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spiderpoul/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spiderpoul/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spiderpoul/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spiderpoul/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spiderpoul","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/commits/186f075e5a1b14592562c07c5501093fd4b4c32e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T20:17:30Z","email":"spiderpoul@mail.ru","name":"Pavel Uvarov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T20:17:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"presentation: rebuild the talk around real repository artifacts (#73)\n\n* presentation: rebuild around real repository artifacts\n\nRestructure the talk so every harness topic is shown as a file from the\ndemo branch followed by best practices and anti-patterns:\n\n- start both demo runs up front and review their results at the end,\n  with short live check-ins along the way;\n- AGENTS.md with a \"what else you touch\" cross-dependency table,\n  a nested AGENTS.md for common/, and a counter-example;\n- agent-friendly docs (current contract, do-not-copy, pitfalls) and a\n  bad-vs-good paragraph;\n- explicit requirements for specs plus the real spec file;\n- the skills in use (log/trace analysis, safe change, UI forms,\n  performance check, code review), skill anatomy, and sharing through\n  the monorepo with CODEOWNERS;\n- subagents: when to use them, a definition file, anti-patterns;\n- checks whose messages act as prompts, and the CI review agent;\n- evals in practice: case, grader, MR template rule, anti-patterns.\n\nSpeaker notes use a plainer voice; places that need the speaker''s own\nexamples are marked TODO instead of inventing them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B4EJbsQcayZ3jP7YvPBS6Q\n\n* presentation: match file excerpts to demo/agent-ready-v2\n\nEvery code excerpt on the slides now matches the committed files in the\nnew demo branch line by line:\n\n- nested common/AGENTS.md and microfrontends.md pitfalls describe what\n  the code actually does (only the react external causes a duplicate\n  React; routePath and entryPath failures as observed in the shell);\n- safe-change description is quoted so the frontmatter stays valid YAML;\n- eval case start commit points at main;\n- log-trace-analysis output is the real run on the committed fixture.\n\nClick-highlight ranges follow the updated excerpts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B4EJbsQcayZ3jP7YvPBS6Q\n\n* presentation: report prompts and the product-local lazy chunk rule\n\n- both demo prompts end with the same request for a short report in\n  agent-report.md, and the results table compares the two reports;\n- the spec excerpt shows the new \"If the lazy chunk does not work\"\n  permission and the shell in out of scope; the spec requirements\n  slide covers scope and permissions;\n- check-in 2 looks for a fix inside the product instead of common/ or\n  the shell, and the notes cite the new check:bundle message.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B4EJbsQcayZ3jP7YvPBS6Q\n\n* presentation: sync the entryPath pitfall with the registry fix\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B4EJbsQcayZ3jP7YvPBS6Q\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fee7ba443478da590f4e958c9e5becf5ad79e4f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/git/trees/fee7ba443478da590f4e958c9e5becf5ad79e4f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/git/commits/186f075e5a1b14592562c07c5501093fd4b4c32e","verification":{"payload":"tree fee7ba443478da590f4e958c9e5becf5ad79e4f2\nparent 64f408a5e656baf140e905add740d61886b3a309\nauthor Pavel Uvarov <spiderpoul@mail.ru> 1790194650 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790194650 +0300\n\npresentation: rebuild the talk around real repository artifacts (#73)\n\n* presentation: rebuild around real repository artifacts\n\nRestructure the talk so every harness topic is shown as a file from the\ndemo branch followed by best practices and anti-patterns:\n\n- start both demo runs up front and review their results at the end,\n  with short live check-ins along the way;\n- AGENTS.md with a \"what else you touch\" cross-dependency table,\n  a nested AGENTS.md for common/, and a counter-example;\n- agent-friendly docs (current contract, do-not-copy, pitfalls) and a\n  bad-vs-good paragraph;\n- explicit requirements for specs plus the real spec file;\n- the skills in use (log/trace analysis, safe change, UI forms,\n  performance check, code review), skill anatomy, and sharing through\n  the monorepo with CODEOWNERS;\n- subagents: when to use them, a definition file, anti-patterns;\n- checks whose messages act as prompts, and the CI review agent;\n- evals in practice: case, grader, MR template rule, anti-patterns.\n\nSpeaker notes use a plainer voice; places that need the speaker''s own\nexamples are marked TODO instead of inventing them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B4EJbsQcayZ3jP7YvPBS6Q\n\n* presentation: match file excerpts to demo/agent-ready-v2\n\nEvery code excerpt on the slides now matches the committed files in the\nnew demo branch line by line:\n\n- nested common/AGENTS.md and microfrontends.md pitfalls describe what\n  the code actually does (only the react external causes a duplicate\n  React; routePath and entryPath failures as observed in the shell);\n- safe-change description is quoted so the frontmatter stays valid YAML;\n- eval case start commit points at main;\n- log-trace-analysis output is the real run on the committed fixture.\n\nClick-highlight ranges follow the updated excerpts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B4EJbsQcayZ3jP7YvPBS6Q\n\n* presentation: report prompts and the product-local lazy chunk rule\n\n- both demo prompts end with the same request for a short report in\n  agent-report.md, and the results table compares the two reports;\n- the spec excerpt shows the new \"If the lazy chunk does not work\"\n  permission and the shell in out of scope; the spec requirements\n  slide covers scope and permissions;\n- check-in 2 looks for a fix inside the product instead of common/ or\n  the shell, and the notes cite the new check:bundle message.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B4EJbsQcayZ3jP7YvPBS6Q\n\n* presentation: sync the entryPath pitfall with the registry fix\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B4EJbsQcayZ3jP7YvPBS6Q\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtDPaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwsgQADLyktGKApif7WcM2Ef03fWZ\niUpzMaPW9PisALDe69kfZF/hNP+N9lVEbewKVLuzAoYGcA0qhOPJrEPRTZs5r3y2\n+xF6qce5SGhtoyNji0C3DZafExI6ERhMDufPaRjodG0NkmxvhXprTt1K511JYjQk\nCI/LA+Votjz0i6LKCkZEE54BOHJCFdMEczLvaSv2mf7S0nwGus8GInRmY9JEeet5\nKQFXNru6j0C+8P8h3YCXd1yYarr0acoQiCEmyiYK6dfAbjOzzRUYSbAw8qivKrOS\nn+dKFzuwT3bNCOUNVfzWSdFfpaD+M/eSxY+A8cnu9uTfWcRoBmbz8IoubAbKT4fq\nakkilWb46q9RxlerF03k9XoEi8pszFG39hpZlkHL2D1y2eRsb8fHg4KCW2kUbRJG\nLV9T+aEoFw2c/lfXUjG6YJIi46oXmzud0kPXO8cRwILb/vCtkUmbAmChSHENeHf8\nvDGteYOq28z1WYiPegRIQHd2FTbqi+bHVFB71iAAW7ZHZR1qJyJ8WNaWCrz1sdya\nOPyXOrvaKXe0FkBkVZJ8opI0xSLugChCCyM6lRkYWxD4exRktXULGtuNFZTpWrV/\nLsTOgrw/3dAn4VfhAC6LcWslapiWxJ2J/jq5kKLSv66Bu3P0/vDomvTyl8olBidS\nCuWVqToQ6/lTMaIBmyQY\n=+XPf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T20:17:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/commit/186f075e5a1b14592562c07c5501093fd4b4c32e","node_id":"C_kwDOP1Nl89oAKDE4NmYwNzVlNWExYjE0NTkyNTYyYzA3YzU1MDEwOTNmZDRiNGMzMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/commit/64f408a5e656baf140e905add740d61886b3a309","sha":"64f408a5e656baf140e905add740d61886b3a309","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/commits/64f408a5e656baf140e905add740d61886b3a309"}],"sha":"186f075e5a1b14592562c07c5501093fd4b4c32e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/commits/186f075e5a1b14592562c07c5501093fd4b4c32e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/commits/64f408a5e656baf140e905add740d61886b3a309/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T12:55:53Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T12:55:53Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix: drop stale microfrontends and isolate failed entries\n\nA microfrontend that had been removed kept coming back and blocked\nevery other product:\n\n- the shell persists its registry to dist/data/microfrontends.json and\n  reloads it on start, and entries left only on an explicit DELETE;\n- a product acknowledged once, so the shell could not tell a live\n  product from a removed one;\n- the client loaded all entries with Promise.all, so one failing\n  import cleared the whole list.\n\nNow products send the acknowledgement as a heartbeat and unregister on\nSIGINT/SIGTERM; the shell drops entries without an acknowledgement for\nMICROFRONTEND_TTL_MS (default 90 s) from the registry, the proxies and\nthe persisted file; the client loads entries with Promise.allSettled,\nwarns about the ones that failed, and wraps product routes in\nMicrofrontendBoundary. Heartbeats re-register the proxy only when the\ndescriptor changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B4EJbsQcayZ3jP7YvPBS6Q","tree":{"sha":"8cf45867170b4799db0280851b91ec2b08c880fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/git/trees/8cf45867170b4799db0280851b91ec2b08c880fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spiderpoul/enterprise-app-optimization/git/commits/64f408a5e656baf140e905add740d61886b3a309","verification":{"payload":"tree 8cf45867170b4799db0280851b91ec2b08c880fa\nparent f9dbc81c90450b05ec63b686eae5a5fb074f7f75\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790168153 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790168153 +0000\n\nfix: drop stale microfrontends and isolate failed entries\n\nA microfrontend that had been removed kept coming back and blocked\nevery other product:\n\n- the shell persists its registry to dist/data/microfrontends.json and\n  reloads it on start, and entries left only on an explicit DELETE;\n- a product acknowledged once, so the shell could not tell a live\n  product from a removed one;\n- the client loaded all entries with Promise.all, so one failing\n  import cleared the whole list.\n\nNow products send the acknowledgement as a heartbeat and unregister on\nSIGINT/SIGTERM; the shell drops entries without an acknowledgement for\nMICROFRONTEND_TTL_MS (default 90 s) from the registry, the proxies and\nthe persisted file; the client loads entries with Promise.allSettled,\nwarns about the ones that failed, and wraps product routes in\nMicrofrontendBoundary. Heartbeats re-register the proxy only when the\ndescriptor changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B4EJbsQcayZ3jP7YvPBS6Q\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNCR9YJJ\nh8Xph1LpfgJBOwmVactc8dCIUcLBeMpfJ8/BqfM242G1vuI5M9ukBA1e58vfVEiyXZoMdCI7jzph\nPAU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T12:55:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/u